<title>ITALY: Italian crude imports up 0.2 pct Jan-July 1996.</title>
<headline>Italian crude imports up 0.2 pct Jan-July 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian imports of crude oil amounted to 41.4 million tonnes in the January to July 1996 period, up 0.2 percent from a year earlier, industry association Unione Petrolifera said in a statement.</p>
<p>Libya accounted for 32.8 percent of imports, Iran 17.5 percent, Saudi Arabia 14.8 percent, the former Soviet Union 12.1 percent and Egypt 5.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
